+# Implementation Plan: Availability Query
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Technical Context
+- Same stack as the rental module: strict TypeScript ESM, Node stdlib only, `node:test`.
+
+## Constitution Check
+- I No runtime deps: pass. II Strict ESM TS: pass, no `any`. III Tests: added to `test/rental.test.ts`, deterministic.
+- IV Explicit rules: reuses `parsePeriod` (period rule) and the overlap rule; the overlap check is extracted into one named helper shared by `book` and `availability`, so the two cannot disagree (SC-002). No unstated rule guessed.
+- V Simplicity: one method, one small helper, no new files.
+Post-design: still passes.
+
+## Design
+- Add `AvailabilityQuery { start, end, kind? }` and `availability(query): string[]` to `RentalService`; export the type from `src/index.ts`.
+- Validate period with `parsePeriod`; if `kind` is not undefined it must be `'board'` or `'sail'`, else throw.
+- Filter equipment by kind and by no overlapping booking; sort with default `Array.prototype.sort()` (code unit order; ids are unique).
+- Read-only.
+
+## Artifacts
+No research, contracts or data-model files: the contract and entity are in the spec. Quickstart: `npm test`.
